<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŭĕrasco</span></b> ,
			ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> [id.]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To attain the age of boyhood</i> or <i>youth</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unus jam puerascens insigni festivitate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to grow young
			again</i> (post-class.), <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 4,
			55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Claud. Mamert. Stat. Anim. 1,
			1</span></i>.</div>
